The function `tcp_find_option` contains the vulnerable option parsing loop. Specifically, in lines 62-66:

	for (i = 0; i < optlen; ) {
		if (op[i] == option) return !invert;
		if (op[i] < 2) i++;
		else i += op[i+1]?:1;
	}

If `i` is equal to `optlen - 1` and `op[i] >= 2`, the code evaluates `op[i+1]`, which is `op[optlen]`. This is an out-of-bounds read because the buffer `op` only has `optlen` elements (valid indices `0` to `optlen - 1`). There is no boundary check to ensure `i + 1 < optlen` before accessing `op[i+1]`.
